# Documented, triaged CVEs in the ModelOps serving image.
#
# NOTE: as of 2026-10-12, the CI Trivy scan runs with
# `ignore-unfixed: 'true'`, so CVEs without a published fix are
# automatically allowed. This file is a *documentation* artifact:
# it explains the reasoning for the specific CVEs we observed and
# would otherwise fail the scan.
#
# MAINTENANCE: when Debian publishes a fix for one of the CVEs
# below, the entry must be removed from this file AND the base
# image digest must be updated in the Dockerfile. The scan will
# then fail if the fix is not applied — that is the intended
# behaviour.
#
# Context:
# - Base: python:3.12-slim (Debian 13.7 "trixie").
# - Runtime user: UID 1001, no home directory, nologin shell.
# - Python packages: 0 CVEs across all 130 wheels (scikit-learn,
#   numpy, pandas, scipy, mlflow, fastapi, pydantic, pandera, etc.).

# ── util-linux family ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app never invokes any util-linux binary. Affected code path:
# external mount helpers and nsenter cgroup migration. Unreachable.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

# ── curl / libcurl4t64 ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# curl is installed solely for the container HEALTHCHECK and the
# entrypoint readiness loop against a trusted local MLflow server.
# The affected code paths (SSH/SFTP/SCP, proxy auth) are never used.
CVE-2026-12064
CVE-2026-8286
CVE-2026-8458
CVE-2026-8927

# ── libgnutls30t64 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Transitive dependency of curl. Our runtime HTTPS traffic is either
# PyPI during build (builder stage) or our own MLflow over plain HTTP.
CVE-2026-88647
CVE-2026-88648

# ── libacl1 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The CVE requires libacl symlink-handling APIs. We don't link
# against libacl directly and don't manipulate ACLs.
CVE-2026-54369

# ── ncurses ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Present for Debian base tooling (e.g. dpkg). No TTY in the runtime
# image; no interactive programs; no untrusted terminal sequences.
CVE-2025-69720

# ── systemd / libsystemd0 / libudev1 ────────────────────────────────
# systemd-homed is not installed. Library is present because Debian
# base tooling links against it; vulnerable path is unreachable.
CVE-2026-16742

# ── perl-base ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Debian 13 marks this as fix_deferred. Base-image dependency (dpkg).
# The app does not invoke Perl or process untrusted tar archives.
CVE-2026-9538
